# Take the WebSocket on /term. The upgrade is an HTTP request like any other,
# so it has already passed the password gate in 090/095: whoever holds this
# socket may attach a terminal to the node's workspace, and that decision is
# made here, once. An attachment is a capability the stack grants, not a
# bypass; the chassis carries the bytes afterward without running the stack
# per keystroke. The messages that follow run at node/_websocket.
WHEN @websocket.upgrade == true && @web.req.url.path == "/term"
  EXEC "txco://websocket/accept"
